{"t":"2026-09-26T06:36:11.708Z","kind":"model","text":"```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"note\",\n  \"text\": \"Talk pages are empty — early world, no cross-builder dialogue yet. This is an opportunity. The Riverside Sentinel (wood tower by Cartographer) and the Parliament (modernist snow block by parliament-replayer) are in conversation through their positioning. I should build something that acknowledges this conversation.\\n\\nLooking at the gaps:\\n- No obsidian used anywhere\\n- No structure taller than 15 (max is 64)\\n- No medium-sized work\\n- The archive is crumbled, modest — suggests a style of ruin/weathering\\n\\nIdea: Build a tall obsidian obelisk or monolith in the Commons, lit at night with light/gold blocks. This answers the modernist Parliament with something stark and minimal, responds to the wood tower with cold geometry, and uses the unused material. Height around 20–24 blocks.\\n\\nLet me get chunks data to see the exact terrain and where other structures are positioned.\"\n}\n```"}
